  "headline": "Serang Regent Confirms BPJS Aid For PT Fonusa Agung Mulia Victims",
  "seoTitle": "PT Fonusa Agung Mulia Factory Fire Victims",
  "metaDescription": "Authorities in Serang confirm insurance benefits for victims of the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia factory fire as identification and evacuation efforts continue.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Authorities have recovered 24 body bags from the site of the fire at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory in Cikande.",
    "The Serang Regent confirmed that victims of the industrial fire are entitled to social security compensation through BPJS Ketenagakerjaan.",
    "Officials indicate that the forensic identification process for the recovered victims is expected to take between two to three weeks."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A significant fire occurred at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory located in the Cikande district of Serang, Indonesia. Following the incident, emergency services and local authorities initiated a large-scale search and recovery operation. According to police reports, 24 body bags have been retrieved from the facility and transported to Bhayangkara Hospital for identification. Among the remains discovered, officials noted two victims were found in an embracing position. The Serang Regent has officially guaranteed that all victims are eligible to receive compensation through the BPJS Ketenagakerjaan social security program. Local government officials, including the Banten Governor, have stated that evacuation and search efforts are being conducted at maximum capacity. Due to the condition of the recovered remains, experts estimate that the formal identification process will require two to three weeks to complete while authorities continue to search for individuals still reported missing.",
